 =?UTF-8?q?=20uniform=20staging=20lands?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

std140 uniform blocks now stage exactly the way the Vulkan raster
does: Ring::stage takes a span at the next_multiple_of alignment with
the capacity bounds, stage_block writes a Block's words little-endian
into the ring's bytes once per batch (the dedupe via the shared
Block's staged_at swap — draws in a row restage for free), and the
write window for the host reads the ring's bytes directly. the test
carries the cycle honestly: gather, stage, dedupe, restage past, the
little-endian bytes asserted after every step.

144 tests green.
